  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2009-p20.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "By symmetry, it is enough to list one representative of each possible triangle shape.\n\nOne complete list of non-congruent possibilities is \\(ABE,\\) \\(ABG,\\) \\(ACE,\\) \\(ABH,\\) \\(AEH,\\) \\(ACF,\\) \\(ACH,\\) and \\(ADF.\\)\n\nEvery other triangle formed from the eight points is congruent to one of these \\(8\\) triangles.\n\nThus, D is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Use symmetry to avoid counting every triangle separately.",
        "Classify triangles by their side lengths after choosing vertices from the two-row array."
      ],
